  "title": "Jabir ibn Hayyan",
  "summary": "Jabir ibn Hayyan is the name attached to a large body of Arabic writings, mostly on alchemy; some lists attribute over three thousand works to him. Sources place him around 721 to 815, in Kufa and at the court of Harun al-Rashid. Historians dispute authorship: many think Isma'ili circles wrote most of the corpus, and some argue he did not exist.",
