  "reviewer_note": "Authorship debate presented per sources: EBSCO (some scholars since the 10th century doubt he existed; many think Isma'ilis wrote most works) and Encyclopedia.com (Sijistani disputed authorship; Ibn al-Nadim noted doubts; Kraus judged the corpus the work of a school, probably 10th century). EBSCO gives Tus as birthplace and also describes Kufa as \"in eastern Persia\", which conflicts; the pin follows Encyclopedia.com's Kufa.",
